            "review_title": "Review at Banh Xeo Em Oi!",
            "review_text": "TheHardings\nWorcester, United Kingdom461 contributions\n1\nYummy Banh xeo\nOct 2018 • Couples\nWe have visited the street market for the last 2 nights. We loved the look of the pancakes as they were being cooked and had already decided to try them today. We were not disappointed .. we had a pork & shrimp and a duck & ginger one .. they are served with a plate of lettuce and basil and a pot of miso . We didn't have a clue on how to eat them and were give. Chopsticks and cutlery and a note on the stall suggested how we eat them. My hubby was given a friendly telling off by mama who instructed him to wrap a little of the pancake in lettuce, dip it and eat it. They are delicious .. worth every penny of £2.80 cost. The staff are super friendly and the beer is ice cold at just 70p. Clean, tidy and cooked in front of you. We also ordered soft shell crab rice wraps and fresh rice paper spring rolls. Give it a go ... You won't be disappointed 🤗\nRead more\nWritten October 15, 2018\nVy Truong\nWow, such a nice and detailed review, for not only our stall but for others travellers as well. Hope you had a great time in Vietnam and see you here soon!\nRead more\nWritten May 9, 2019\nThis response is the subjective opinion of the management representative and not of Tripadvisor LLC nor of its partners.",
